              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to knock, then the Marathi for to compare."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: फिरायला जाणे",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फिरायला जाणे — phirāylā jāṇe — \"to go for a walk\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फिरायला is \"for wandering\", from फिरणे, \"to wander, turn\", which CDIAL lists under a reconstructed phirati, \"moves, wanders\" (CDIAL 9078). जाणे comes from Sanskrit yāti, \"goes\" (CDIAL 10452)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
